    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0511" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1947v03/pg493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.6362/3–1147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gallman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-11T19:00:00+00:00">March 11, 1947—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1566. This is Salco 445. Possibility of UK seeking import US coal still receiving
                    Cabinet consideration. However, we do not anticipate <pb facs="0512" n="494"
                        xml:id="pg494"/> reversal previous decision unless dollar shortages other
                    ECO countries prevent them from taking all US availability. In that case,
                    possible UK may buy surplus for purpose building stocks.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d283-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gallman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d283-f1" n="1" xml:id="d283-f1-content">
                <p>Chargé Gallman in telegram 1648 (Salco 451), March 14, from London, reported:
                    “British Cabinet decided today request ECO for allocation US coal to UK.”
                    (840.6362/3–1447)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
